      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is true. The vectors $t$ and $s$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $t$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $s$. So, $t=3s$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $p$ and $q$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $p$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $q$. So, $p\\ne 2q$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $r$ and $p$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $r$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $p$. So, $r=-p$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
