    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1813778b-6cec-5323-9caa-e693d0bdae69",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186096700/assets/55662dad06e3011e0efd79d8a7aa539bfffe74bbdc83f308364692b1daa7a370.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is true. The vectors $a$ and $c$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $a=-c$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $c$ and $a$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $c$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $c\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}a$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $b$ and $d$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $b$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $b\\ne d$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f7dec0a7-8847-5321-be8e-065668236ee5",
          ":answer-field/key": "$a=-c$",
