      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $a$ and $c$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $a\\ne -2c$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $b$ and $d$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $b$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $b\\ne -d$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $a$ and $c$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $a=2c$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
