    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7bf1e40c-1f04-5733-955b-5a4f5924df99",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186096700/assets/2f91dafd8d2eed5315af7f799803897ce7dbb7aec1bf75618656372faaae864b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $t=3r$\n\nII. $s=2q$\n\nIII. $p=-s$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is true. The vectors $t$ and $r$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $t$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $r$. So, $t=3r$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $s$ and $q$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $s$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $q$. So, $s\\ne 2q$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $p$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $s$. So, $p\\ne -s$.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "09ebc0b7-cc22-5e6e-88b0-6ade9dfc3eeb",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
