      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186096700/assets/fe8aaf7694b7049c4f61c48bda634231301e4055539674698628edf954ac0126.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $c$ and $d$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $c$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $c\\ne -d$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $d$ and $c$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $d=-\\frac{1}{2}c$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $a$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $a\\ne b$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
