      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $a$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $a\\ne -b$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $b$ and $a$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $b$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $b\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}a$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $c$ and $d$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $c$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $c=d$.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
