    "question": {
      ":question/id": "27f8f58a-835f-5bb6-98f8-b8fa54bcbf12",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186096700/assets/947cca253d410293c697c9d8ce71d0ba1271072014b0392781ea9304a9426de8.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $e$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $e\\ne -b$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $b$ and $e$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $b$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $b=-\\frac{1}{2}e$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $c$ and $a$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $c$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $c\\ne a$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
