      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is true. The vectors $a$ and $d$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $d$. So, $a=-d$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $d$ and $a$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $d\\ne -\\frac{1}{2}a$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $e$ and $b$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $e$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $e=b$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
